        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. Concept of Central Bank Autonomy:\nPursuant to Section 3 of the Nepal Rastra Bank Act, 2058, the central bank is established as an **autonomous, corporate body with perpetual succession**. Central bank autonomy signifies operational and statutory independence from government or political interference in formulating and executing monetary, foreign exchange, and financial supervisory mandates.\n\n2. Statutory Safeguards in NRB Act, 2058:\n\n• **Institutional Autonomy (Sec 3):** Own common seal, full capacity to acquire and dispose of movable/immovable assets, and power to sue and be sued in its corporate name.\n\n• **Security of Tenure for Leadership (Sec 21 & 22):** The Governor, Deputy Governors, and Directors hold fixed 5-year terms and cannot be arbitrarily dismissed without a formal Inquiry Committee chaired by a retired Supreme Court Justice finding gross misconduct or incapacity.\n\n• **Functional Policy Autonomy:** Sole statutory authority to formulate, implement, and regulate monetary policy, interest rate corridors, and foreign exchange regimes without cabinet veto.\n\n• **Financial Autonomy (Sec 28):** Self-budgeting authority, with strict statutory caps limiting direct overdraft lending to the Government of Nepal (maximum 10% of previous year's government revenues).\n\n***Conclusion:*** Autonomy is the vital prerequisite for price and financial stability, balanced by statutory reporting accountability to the national parliament.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. अवधारणा (Concept of Central Bank Autonomy):\nनेपाल राष्ट्र बैंक ऐन, २०५८ को दफा ३ अनुसार नेपाल राष्ट्र बैंक एक **अविच्छिन्न उत्तराधिकारवाला, स्वशासित र संगठित (Autonomous Body with Perpetual Succession)** केन्द्रीय बैंक हो। स्वायत्तता भन्नाले सरकार वा बाह्य राजनीतिक हस्तक्षेप बिना मूल्य स्थायित्व, बाह्य क्षेत्र स्थायित्व र वित्तीय प्रणालीको नियमन सम्बन्धी निर्णय स्वतन्त्र रूपमा गर्न पाउने कानुनी अधिकार हो।\n\n२. स्वायत्तता सुनिश्चित गर