      ModelQuestion(
        number: 2,
        questionText: "What are the main components included in Tier 1 [Core] Capital and Tier 2 [Supplementary] Capital?",
        questionTextNepali: "प्राथमिक पूँजी (Tier 1 Capital) र पूरक पूँजी (Tier 2 Capital) मा समावेश हुने प्रमुख तत्वहरू के-के हुन्?",
        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. Introduction:\nUnder Nepal Rastra Bank's Capital Adequacy Framework (aligned with Basel III standards), a bank's total capital fund is categorized into **Tier 1 (Core Capital)** and **Tier 2 (Supplementary Capital)** to act as a resilient financial cushion against systemic shocks.\n\n2. Key Components Breakdown:\n\n• **A) Tier 1 Capital (Core / Common Equity Tier 1 - CET1):**\n\n- Definition: The highest quality, permanent, unencumbered capital that absorbs operating losses on a going-concern basis.\n\n- Elements: 1. Paid-up Equity Share Capital, 2. Proposed Bonus Shares, 3. Statutory General Reserve, 4. Share Premium, 5. Retained Earnings, 6. Capital Redemption Reserve. (Mandatory regulatory deductions: Intangible assets/goodwill, deferred tax assets, and cross-holding investments).\n\n• **B) Tier 2 Capital (Supplementary Capital):**\n\n- Definition: Secondary-grade capital providing gone-concern loss absorbency during severe distress or institutional resolution.\n\n- Elements: 1. General Loan Loss Provisions on Pass loans (capped at maximum 1.25% of total Credit Risk Weighted Assets), 2. Asset Revaluation Reserves (discounted up to 2%), 3. Subordinated Term Debentures (with minimum 5-year remaining maturity and progressive straight-line amortization), 4. Hybrid debt capital instruments.\n\nTotal Capital Adequacy Ratio (CAR) = [ (Tier 1 + Tier 2) / Total Risk Weighted Assets ] × 100 ≥ 11.00%\n\n***Conclusion:*** Tier 1 capital insulates banks during ordinary operations, while Tier 2 guarantees depositor restitution in resolution scenarios.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. परिचय (Introduction):\nनेपाल राष्ट्र बैंकको पूँजी पर्याप्तता ढाँचा (Capital Adequacy Framework - Basel III) अनुसार बैंकको कुल जोखिम भारित सम्पत्ति (RWA) सँग सन्तुलन मिलाउन कायम गरिने कुल पुँजी कोषलाई **प्राथमिक पूँजी (Tier 1)** र **पूरक पूँजी (Tier 2)** मा विभाजन गरिएको छ।\n\n२. पुँजी कोषका प्रमुख घटकहरू (Key Components):\n\n• **क) प्राथमिक पूँजी / कोर क्यापिटल (Tier 1 / Common Equity Tier 1 - CET1):**\n\n- यो बैंकको उच्चतम गुणस्तरको, स्थायी प्रकृतिको र नोक्सानी सोस्ने (Loss-absorbing) प्राथमिक पुँजी हो।\n\n- घटकहरू: १. चुक्ता पुँजी (Paid-up Equity Capital), २. प्रस्तावित बोनस सेयर, ३. साधारण जगेडा कोष (General Reserve), ४. सेयर प्रिमियम (Share Premium), ५. सञ्चित मुनाफा (Retained Earnings), ६. पुँजी फिर्ता जगेडा कोष (Capital Redemption Reserve)। (घटाउनुपर्ने: अमूर्त सम्पत्ति, डिफर्ड ट्याक्स, लगानी समायोजन)\n\n• **ख) पूरक पूँजी (Tier 2 / Supplementary Capital):**\n\n- यो द्वितीयक स्तरको, संकटका बेला मात्र प्रयोग गर्न सकिने पूरक पुँजी हो।\n\n- घटकहरू: १. असल कर्जा नोक्सानी व्यवस्था (General Loan Loss Provision - RWA को अधिकतम १.२५% सम्म), २. सम्पत्ति पुनर्मूल्यांकन जगेडा (Revaluation Reserves - अधिकतम २%), ३. हाइब्रिड पुँजी उपकरणहरू, ४. अविमोच्य प्राथमिकता सेयर, ५. अधीनस्थ आवधिक ऋण (Subordinated Term Debt - ५ वर्ष भन्दा बढी अवधिको ऋणपत्र)।\n\nकुल पुँजी कोष (Total Capital Fund) = प्राथमिक पूँजी (Tier 1) + पूरक पूँजी (Tier 2) ≥ ११.००% (Total CAR)\n\n***निष्कर्ष:*** प्राथमिक पुँजीले नियमित सञ्चालनमा हुने नोक्सानी व्यहोर्छ भने पूरक पुँजीले बैंक लिक्विडेसनमा जाँदा निक्षेपकर्ताको सुरक्षा गर्दछ।",
